Okay, so I need to figure out how many miles Emberly has walked in March. She walks every day except for 4 days, and each walk is 1 hour covering 4 miles. March typically has 31 days, right? So first, I'll calculate how many days she actually walked. That's 31 minus 4, which equals 27 days. Each day she walks 4 miles, so multiplying 27 days by 4 miles per day gives me 108 miles. That seems straightforward. I think I've got it.
</think>

